  "question": {
    "text": "The lines $2 \\mathrm{x}-3 \\mathrm{y}=5$ and $3 \\mathrm{x}-4 \\mathrm{y}=7$ are diameters of a circle having area as 154 sq. units. Then the equation of the circle is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "xj0Tn",
      "text": "\n$x^2+y^2-2 x+2 y=62$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jmGVE",
      "text": "\n$x^2+y^2+2 x-2 y=62$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "18vac",
      "text": "\n$x^2+y^2+2 x-2 y=47$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "veOQa",
      "text": "\n$x^2+y^2-2 x+2 y=47$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\pi \\mathrm{r}^2=154 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{r}=7$\nFor centre on solving equation\n$2 x-3 y=5 \\quad \\& \\quad 3 x-4 y=7 \\text { or } x=1, y=1 \\text { centre }=(1,-1)$\nEquation of circle, $(\\mathrm{x}-1)^2+(\\mathrm{y}+1)^2=7^2$\n$x^2+y^2-2 x+2 y=47$",
    "image": null
  },
